WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.075
Reading the findings is
where the rules become real.

2
00:00:03.075 --> 00:00:07.481
Seven rows are standing privilege in
the top tiers, including a service

3
00:00:07.481 --> 00:00:11.813
principal whose exception nobody
owns, so the exception doesn't count.

4
00:00:11.813 --> 00:00:14.975
One Global Administrator
also elevated to root.

5
00:00:14.975 --> 00:00:19.204
There are five Global Administrators
once the group's members are counted,

6
00:00:19.204 --> 00:00:21.250
and five owners on one subscription.

7
00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.093
The emergency account
is only informational,

8
00:00:24.093 --> 00:00:26.862
because it's a listed
exception with an owner.

9
00:00:26.862 --> 00:00:31.301
Then you watch the reader refuse an
undeclared call and an unknown cloud.

10
00:00:31.301 --> 00:00:34.460
The whole suite passes,
three hundred thirty tests.
